data: {"run_id":"b939b22f3a734cb8846ba1f763bda9c4","seq":10,"stage":"respond","status":"ok","parent":null,"label":"10","data":{"action":"answer","system":"You are a career agent inside a job-search product. Answer the user's career question helpfully and concretely. Keep the answer under 200 words.","max_tokens":300,"max_chars":1500,"provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","text":"# CV Review for Senior Analyst Role\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Solid technical foundation (SQL, Python, Statistics degree)\n- Quantified impact (30% efficiency gain) – excellent\n- 4 years relevant experience shows progression potential\n\n**Areas to strengthen:**\n\n1. **Expand beyond dashboards**: Senior roles need broader analytics. Highlight any A/B testing, statistical modeling, forecasting, or business strategy work.\n\n2. **Business impact**: Translate technical wins into business outcomes. Did that 30% time savings save costs? Enable better decisions?\n\n3. **Leadership/mentoring**: Any team collaboration, training junior analysts, or cross-functional projects? Senior roles expect this.\n\n4. **Advanced skills**: Consider adding machine learning, cloud platforms (AWS/GCP), or advanced statistical methods if applicable.\n\n5. **Certifications/continuous learning**: Any recent courses or certifications?\n\n**Quick wins:**\n- Add 2-3 bullet points showing business context, not just technical metrics\n- Include a brief summary positioning you for senior-level strategic work\n- Quantify team impact if relevant\n\n**Verdict**: You have a solid foundation, but need to demonstrate readiness for strategic responsibility, not just technical execution. Focus your CV on *decisions you enabled*, not just reports you built.","truncated":false,"recorded_at":"2026-10-29T14:33:49+00:00","replayed":true},"ms":3988,"tokens":403,"cost_usd":0.001547}

